  "market_context": "Gold was in a clear downtrend on the 15-minute chart. Price formed a descending triangle pattern with a flat support level around 2288–2290 and a descending resistance trendline connecting lower highs. The market tested the support multiple times before breaking it decisively.",
  "key_observation": "Price broke the horizontal support of the descending triangle to the downside, confirming bearish continuation; support then acted as resistance, and a bearish engulfing candle provided the entry trigger for a short.",
  "analysis_steps": [
    "Step 1: Identified a descending triangle pattern within an existing downtrend on the Gold 15-minute chart, bounded by a flat support zone (~2288–2290) and a descending resistance trendline.",
    "Step 2: Observed price breaking below the support level decisively, signaling bearish momentum and continuation of the downtrend.",
    "Step 3: Noted that the broken support now functioned as resistance, creating a high-probability short zone.",
    "Step 4: Used the bearish engulfing candlestick (closing below prior candle’s open and low) as the specific entry confirmation for the short position.",
    "Step 5: Placed stop loss above the high of the engulfing candle and set a 1:2 risk-to-reward target."
  ],
  "outcome": "Short trade executed after breakdown and bearish engulfing candle; price continued downward confirming the bearish continuation. (No explicit P/L stated, but outcome described as successful continuation.)",
  "lessons": "Descending triangles in downtrends often signal continuation; a clean break of support combined with a strong reversal candle (e.g., bearish engulfing) provides high-probability short entries with clear risk management.",
